<BaseLayout current="Essays" title="Why I Am Starting This Journey">
  <article class="prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">ESSAY · INTRODUCTION</div><h1>Why I Am Starting This Journey</h1><p class="small-note">A note on curiosity, research, engineering and learning in public.</p>
    <p>I have always been fascinated by the process of understanding things. Not just knowing how something works, but understanding why it works, what principles govern it, where its limitations lie, and whether it could be improved.</p>
    <p>I enjoy reading, learning, investigating complex subjects and exploring ideas that connect different fields. A question can lead to a scientific paper. A paper can lead to another question. An apparently simple problem can open the door to an entire field of knowledge.</p>
    <h2>From curiosity to understanding</h2>
    <p>I am particularly interested in engineering, advanced manufacturing, materials science, robotics and intelligent systems. What connects these subjects for me is the possibility of turning abstract knowledge into something tangible.</p>
    <p>A mathematical model can help explain a physical phenomenon. A better understanding of materials can lead to a more reliable component. A new mechanical design can make a machine lighter, stronger or more efficient.</p>
    <h2>Learning in public</h2>
    <p>I am not starting this website because I believe I already have all the answers. I am starting because I have many questions, and I want to become better at investigating them.</p>
    <p>I will write about scientific papers I read, concepts I find difficult, engineering problems I explore, experiments I conduct and ideas that deserve further investigation. I will try to distinguish what is established from what I think might be true.</p>
    <h2>An interest in building things</h2>
    <p>One of my long-term ambitions is to contribute to the development of a robotics and innovation laboratory in Togo. I imagine a place where people can study scientific ideas, design mechanical systems, experiment with robotics, develop prototypes and learn by solving real problems.</p>
    <p>Building such a place requires scientific foundations, engineering skills, practical experience, collaboration and an understanding of the industrial environment. I want this website to become part of that journey.</p>
    <h2>A long-term project</h2>
    <p>I do not know exactly where this journey will lead. For now, the commitment is simple: read carefully, think independently, write clearly, build things, test assumptions and share what I learn.</p>
    <p><strong>Ideas, questions and things worth understanding.</strong></p>
  </article>
